482
00:49:50,419 --> 00:49:58,596
We can convince ourselves that programs indeed are totally correct.

483
00:50:04,273 --> 00:50:11,238
Please realize that if you have written a program

484
00:50:14,855 --> 00:50:16,096
and it's not correct,

485
00:50:19,933 --> 00:50:26,338
That is a little bit cowardly to say that your program had a bug.

486
00:50:29,572 --> 00:50:40,779
To call errors, bugs is a very primitive animistic attitude.

487
00:50:40,779 --> 00:50:46,560
Suggests that that, that the bug has a life of itself.

488
00:50:46,560 --> 00:50:51,117
That you're not totally responsible for it, the mean little bug

489
00:50:52,249 --> 00:50:55,056
crept in behind your back.

490
00:50:55,056 --> 00:50:55,256
At the moment, you were not looking.

491
00:50:55,256 --> 00:51:03,499
Yah, now this is not true if the program is not correct.

492
00:51:03,499 --> 00:51:13,980
You made an error and my request, my prayer so to speak, is.

493
00:51:13,980 --> 00:51:18,976
That you stop using the term bugs for program errors, but

494
00:51:18,976 --> 00:51:21,432
call them what they are Errors

495
00:51:25,952 --> 00:51:37,280
unless we change our language and call an error and error.

496
00:51:37,280 --> 00:51:40,140
Programming and computing science have not yet matured.

497
00:51:40,140 --> 00:51:42,263
Thank you for your attention.

